# Sanitized source snapshot for Dockerfile.e2e (issue #204).
#
# This file is an ALLOWLIST, not a blocklist. `*` excludes the entire build
# context and each `!` line adds back one directory or file the E2E image
# genuinely needs. A blocklist would silently ship every new secret-shaped file
# somebody drops in the worktree; an allowlist fails the build instead, which is
# the direction we want to be wrong in.
#
# What must never reach the image: `.git` (history, remotes, credential
# helpers), `.env*` (real tokens), `.state/` (this machine's notification
# history and pins), host `node_modules` (wrong platform for a Linux container),
# and every generated report/screenshot directory.
*

# --- build + test inputs -----------------------------------------------------
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!tsconfig.server.json
!tsconfig.tools.json
!vite.config.ts
!vitest.config.ts
!playwright.config.ts
!playwright.docker.config.ts
!playwright.preview.config.ts
!opencode.json
!client
!server
!tests
!scripts

# --- Markdown compiled into the SPA by client/lib/docs.ts --------------------
# These are `?raw` imports, so a missing one is a Vite build failure, not a
# runtime 404. docs/, deploy/README.md and reminders/README.md are all reachable
# from the in-app docs catalogue.
!README.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!AGENTS.md
!LICENSE
!docs
!deploy
!reminders

# --- re-exclusions ------------------------------------------------------------
# Last match wins, so these run after the allowlist above and strip anything
# sensitive or machine-local that lives *inside* a re-included directory.
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.state
**/.projects
**/dist
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/screenshot-output
**/screenshots-out
**/pr-preview-output
**/docker-e2e-artifacts
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/mcp-servers.json
**/.agent-status.json
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
